@startuml generated-drivers-two-ladders
' ============================================================================
' The 2x2 experiment that identified the cross-type hop as THE mechanism behind
' eight sloped generated drivers.  MEASURED 2026-07-29, RLIMIT_STACK bisection.
'   RED   #C62828 sloped — a live defect
'   GREEN #2E7D32 flat
'   TEAL  #00695C control
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4

title <b>Two ladders, nine generated drivers</b>\nthe cross-type hop is the mechanism — confirmed 9 for 9

rectangle "**LADDER A — ALTERNATING CATEGORIES**\n`nested_list`: ``Proc::CastList(Arc<List>)`` then ``List::ListLit(Vec<Proc>)``\nthe hop is crossed at EVERY level" as A #FFEBEE {
  card "`ast_cmp`             **10,592.4** / **335.3**" as a1 #EF9A9A
  card "`ast_debug`           **10,544.2** / **463.8**" as a2 #EF9A9A
  card "`ast_eq`               **6,144.0** / **175.7**" as a3 #EF9A9A
  card "`ast_normalize`        **6,144.0** / **176.7**" as a4 #EF9A9A
  card "`ast_match_pattern`    **6,138.0** / **174.7**" as a5 #EF9A9A
  card "`ast_subst`            **6,134.0** / **174.7**" as a6 #EF9A9A
  card "`ast_hash`             **1,216.8** / **206.8**" as a7 #EF9A9A
  card "`ast_semantic_hash`    **1,214.7** / **206.8**" as a8 #EF9A9A
  card "`ast_drop`               **254.0** /  **96.4**\n<i>the one pre-existing subject — reproduced to the byte</i>" as a9 #EF5350
  card "`ast_display`                **0.0** /   **0**\n★ FLAT — its driver DOES follow the hop" as a10 #A5D6A7
  card "`ast_clone`                  **2.0** /   **0**\n★ FLAT — it does not traverse at all" as a11 #66BB6A
  card "`build_twins` (control)      **1.0** /   **0**" as a12 #80CBC4
}

rectangle "**LADDER B — PURE SINGLE CATEGORY**\n`nested_add`: ``Proc::Add(Arc<Proc>, Arc<Proc>)``\nno hop exists to cross" as B #E8F5E9 {
  card "**every one of the nine: <latex>\approx 0</latex> B/level**\n`ast_cmp` `ast_debug` `ast_eq` `ast_normalize`\n`ast_match_pattern` `ast_subst` `ast_hash`\n`ast_semantic_hash` `ast_display` `ast_drop`" as b1 #A5D6A7
  card "`build_twins_add` (control)  <latex>\approx 0</latex>" as b2 #80CBC4
}

A -[#455A64,thickness=3]right-> B : the ONLY difference is the SHAPE walked

note bottom of A #FFEBEE
  ★★ **Eight sloped drivers are a LIVE DEFECT class in `macros/src/gen/`**, not a
  documentation gap: depth-independence is these modules' entire purpose.
  Figures are **debug / release** B/level, ladder <latex>16 \rightarrow 4{,}096</latex>,
  bisected at 4 KiB resolution on the child's MAIN thread.
end note

note bottom of B #E8F5E9
  The controls are flat on **both** ladders, so every slope in ladder A is the
  **driver's own** and not the builder's or the harness's.
  <latex>\Rightarrow</latex> The generated work stacks are typed **per category** and do not
  follow an edge that leaves their own type.
end note

legend bottom
  |= cell |= meaning |
  |<#EF9A9A>| sloped on the alternating ladder — the defect |
  |<#A5D6A7>| flat |
  |<#66BB6A>| flat by REPRESENTATION (<latex>\mathtt{Arc::clone}</latex>), not by a driver |
  |<#80CBC4>| control — runs no driver |
endlegend

@enduml
